{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["This is that which pertains to the Levites — a new commandment that had not yet been stated: in the section of the census at Sinai and in the section of Naso, the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded to count them from age thirty to age fifty, to do the work and the carrying, to carry the Tabernacle. And now in this section He comes to explain the commandment of guard-duty service of the Tabernacle: that five years before the age of thirty, when he is not fit for carrying, he shall be fit and commanded for guarding the Tabernacle and its vessels. And from age fifty and upward, when he is no longer fit for the work of carrying, he shall be commanded for the work of guarding, as He proceeds to explain." "From age twenty-five years and upward he shall come to serve in the service of the Tent of Meeting — the work of guarding, as He explains right after: וְשֵׁרֵת אֶת אֶחָיו לִשְׁמֹר מִשְׁמֶרֶת."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:54.105894762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}